# AEGIS ignore file (design doc §16). Copy to `.aegisignore` in a folder you
# scan (or in $HOME). One pattern per line. A bare word matches both a
# directory anywhere in the tree and a file of that name, so you don't need to
# learn glob syntax:
#
#   proofs          ->  skips */proofs/* AND a file named "proofs"
#   *.iso           ->  skips ISO images
#
# Lines starting with # are comments. AEGIS never scans this file itself.

# build / dependency trees a security scan usually shouldn't walk file-by-file
# (note: node_modules is exactly where supply-chain malware hides, so excluding
# it is a trade-off you are choosing — see `--skip-dev-noise`)
node_modules
.venv
__pycache__
target
.git

# large opaque artifacts that read as high-entropy by nature (§7)
*.iso
*.dmg

# AEGIS's own generated corpus of malware fixtures, if you ran make-corpus here
corpus

# AEGIS's own package files necessarily contain attack-command strings and the
# EICAR string as fixtures/documentation (the "tool meets itself" case, §8/§18).
# Skip AEGIS trees so copies of the scanner in your Downloads don't self-flag.
aegis-project
aegis_pkg
aegis-antivirus
aegis-av
AEGIS-design*.md
DESIGN.md
rules.example
